# Maintainer: Genesi OS Team <dev@genesios.org>
#
# Genesi Studio Mode — give the whole machine to one app.
#
# The focused app (or apps — several may be focused at once) gets negative nice,
# the fastest cores, a 4x cgroup CPU/IO share and the performance governor,
# while every other OPEN APPLICATION is frozen so it cannot steal a cycle.
# Frozen means paused, not closed: cgroup v2 `cgroup.freeze` (SIGSTOP as a
# fallback) stops the process being scheduled while it keeps its memory and its
# unsaved work. Turning Studio Mode off — manually, or automatically when the
# focused app exits — thaws everything and restores every lever it touched.
#
# THREE PROCESSES, ONE CONTROL PATH
#   genesi-studiod         per-user daemon: windows, freezing, restore, state
#   genesi-studio-helperd  root helper: the privileged levers only, SO_PEERCRED-
#                          authenticated so a caller can only touch its own pids
#   genesi-studio          CLI every UI drives (plasmoid, tray, GNOME extension)
#
# DESKTOP COVERAGE
#   The window list is per-compositor, so genesi_studio_wm.py carries a backend
#   for each: hyprctl (Hyprland/caelestia), niri msg, swaymsg, a KWin script
#   over DBus (Plasma Wayland), EWMH via wmctrl (Xfce/Cinnamon/Budgie/LXDE and
#   any X11 session), and a /proc scan as the always-works fallback.
#
#   The UI follows the same shape: a Plasma 6 plasmoid on KDE, a GNOME Shell
#   extension on GNOME (which is also what gives GNOME Wayland real focus
#   detection — Mutter exposes none to outside processes), and a libappindicator
#   tray everywhere else, including Cosmic via cosmic-panel's status area.
pkgname=genesi-studio
pkgver=1.0.0
# pkgrel 2: make wmctrl/xorg-xprop hard deps (without them a KDE X11 session
# silently fell back to the /proc scan and listed daemons instead of windows),
# resolve real app icons and names from .desktop entries for every widget, and
# make the /proc backend require an open display-server connection so the app
# picker on COSMIC and GNOME Wayland lists applications rather than agents.
# pkgrel 3: multi-app selection in both widgets (the picker used to fire on the
# first click, so a second app could never be chosen), a desktop notification on
# switch-on/off reporting how many apps were paused (Studio Mode was otherwise
# invisible — a frozen window keeps its last frame on screen), and /proc app
# identity by real executable instead of comm, which is truncated at 15 chars
# and rewritten per-child by Electron apps.
# pkgrel 4: THE fix for "Backend: procfs, nothing found". genesi-studiod is a
# systemd --user service and so has no DISPLAY/WAYLAND_DISPLAY of its own — every
# real backend failed available() and the session dropped to procfs. It now
# harvests the session env from a compositor process before detecting. Also
# reverts the pkgrel-3 display-socket app filter, which was broken (a client's
# socket fd inode never matches the server's listening inode → empty list) back
# to desktop-entry matching + the NoDisplay veto.
# pkgrel 5: fix "the focused app feels laggier with Studio on". The -10 nice
# starved the compositor (the app won CPU over kwin/mutter, so its own window
# repainted less) and fought ananicy-cpp; it is now -5, with cgroup cpu.weight
# as the real lever. CPU-affinity pinning is now hybrid-only: on a uniform CPU
# or a VM it pinned the app to a core subset and made it slower, so it is a
# no-op there now. X11 backend reads real WM_CLASS (wmctrl -lxp) so apps whose
# comm is generic (the Qt Monitor, the Electron editor) still get name + icon.
# pkgrel 6: a window with an empty title produced 5 wmctrl fields instead of 6
# and the parser dropped the whole line, so those windows never appeared in the
# picker. Accept 5 and blank the title. Adds X11-parsing test coverage.
# pkgrel 7: THE reason every session ran on procfs. list_windows() demoted the
# backend permanently after three empty polls — and the daemon starts at login,
# before any window exists, so every session burned its three strikes in six
# seconds and was stuck listing daemons with no focus tracking until a manual
# restart. Empty is a legitimate answer; the fallback is now per-call and
# recoverable. Also fixes the systemd "Unknown key 'StartLimitIntervalSec' in
# section [Service]" warning (it belongs in [Unit]).
# pkgrel 8: `wmctrl -lxp` columns are id, desktop, PID, WM_CLASS — the parser
# had PID and WM_CLASS swapped, so int() raised on every line, the X11 backend
# returned nothing, and the session fell to procfs every time. Verified against
# real session output, which is now the test fixture. Also folds '_' to '-' when
# matching desktop entries (Qt names the AI Monitor's WM_CLASS
# "Genesi_ai_monitor" but its entry is genesi-ai-monitor), and stops .desktop
# launchers that merely run a terminal from claiming the terminal's identity.
# pkgrel 9: a window that never sets _NET_WM_PID (some toolkits, some Electron
# builds) came back from wmctrl with pid 0 and was dropped, hiding a real app.
# Recover the process by matching the window class instead.
# pkgrel 10: real app icons in the picker. Matching kept only the last WM_CLASS
# component, throwing away the exact key an entry is indexed under (Genesi Code
# declares StartupWMClass=dev.genesi.GenesiCode), and "GenesiCode" never met
# genesi-code because the two differ only in punctuation. The full class is now
# matched, with a separator-insensitive fallback pass. Shell/compositor windows
# are also flagged so the widgets stop offering plasmashell as a target.
# pkgrel 11: stronger boost (memory.swap.max=0 and memory.low so the focused app
# is never paged out or reclaimed — the biggest remaining source of stutter —
# plus 10x cgroup weight, vm.swappiness and GPU performance level), a green
# outline around focused windows on X11 via genesi-studio-outline (KWin has no
# API to tint another window's decoration, so it is drawn), and a white panel
# icon (the plasmoid was not masking it, so `color` never applied).
# pkgrel 12: THROTTLE background apps (renice +19 + ionice idle) instead of
# freezing them by default. A frozen Wayland client cannot answer the
# compositor's ping, so Hyprland/KWin/Mutter marked it "not responding" and
# popped a wait/force-quit dialog over every paused app — reported on Hyprland +
# caelestia. Throttling keeps them alive-enough to pong while giving the focused
# app the machine. True freeze stays available via `suspend_method=freeze`.
# pkgrel 13: the boost reached one thread of the app and stood down from the GPU.
# nice/ionice/affinity are per-thread on Linux, so setting them on the tgid moved
# the main thread and nothing else — measured on Firefox, 1 of 113 threads — and a
# game renders off its main thread, which made the whole per-process boost close
# to a no-op. They now cover every thread. AI Mode ownership is per lever instead
# of all-or-nothing: a warm ollama used to disable EVERY global knob including the
# GPU, the one lever a game actually feels. And the cgroup levers now require the
# app to have a cgroup to itself — an app launched from the compositor sits in the
# shared session-N.scope, where cpu.weight raises the group against itself and the
# memory knobs rewrite the whole session's policy. Also forces LC_ALL=C when
# reading ionice: a localised "prioridade 4" did not match the priority pattern,
# so restore put the app back on the right class at the wrong priority.
# pkgrel 14: the pkgrel-13 cgroup check rejected the app's OWN scope. It asked
# whether every process in the cgroup descends from the boosted pid, but that pid
# is usually a leaf: Minecraft's scope is rooted at the launcher script with java
# several levels below it, so the levers were skipped for exactly the app they
# were meant for. The test is on the cgroup's shape now — members whose parent is
# not also a member are roots, and one root means one app.
pkgrel=14
pkgdesc='Genesi Studio Mode: focus one app, freeze the rest, restore everything after'
arch=('any')
url='https://github.com/Genesi-OS/GenesiOS'
license=('AGPL-3.0-or-later')
depends=(
    'python'
    'systemd'
    # HARD deps, not optional — learned the hard way on a KDE X11 install:
    # with these missing the EWMH backend declares itself unavailable and the
    # session silently falls back to the /proc scan, which lists daemons
    # (kded6, plasmashell, kaccess) instead of the user's actual windows and
    # loses focus tracking entirely. X11 is the default session on Plasma here,
    # so the "optional" backend was in fact the primary one. Both are tiny.
    'wmctrl'
    'xorg-xprop'
    # ionice, for the I/O priority lever.
    'util-linux'
)
optdepends=(
    'libnotify: desktop notification when Studio Mode switches on or off'
    'pyside6: green outline around the focused window on X11 desktops'
    'nvidia-settings: PowerMizer maximum-performance mode on NVIDIA GPUs'
    'python-gobject: system-tray widget (non-KDE, non-GNOME desktops)'
    'libayatana-appindicator: system-tray widget (the proven SNI path in Genesi)'
    'gtk3: system-tray widget'
    'plasma-workspace: the Plasma 6 Studio Mode widget'
    'gnome-shell: the GNOME Studio Mode extension'
)
install='genesi-studio.install'
source=()
sha256sums=()

check() {
    # The freeze-safety rules decide whether background apps merely pause or the
    # desktop locks up with no way to turn Studio Mode back off, so they are
    # tested at build time. Pure logic, no session required.
    python "${startdir}/test-studio-safety.py"
}

package() {
    # ── executables ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    install -Dm755 "${startdir}/genesi-studiod" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/bin/genesi-studiod"
    install -Dm755 "${startdir}/genesi-studio-helperd" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/bin/genesi-studio-helperd"
    install -Dm755 "${startdir}/genesi-studio" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/bin/genesi-studio"
    install -Dm755 "${startdir}/genesi-studio-tray" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/bin/genesi-studio-tray"
    install -Dm755 "${startdir}/genesi-studio-outline" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/bin/genesi-studio-outline"

    # ── shared library ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Both daemons import this; it lives outside /usr/bin so it is never on PATH.
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/genesi_studio_wm.py" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/share/genesi-studio/genesi_studio_wm.py"

    # ── systemd units ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/genesi-studiod.service" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/lib/systemd/user/genesi-studiod.service"
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/genesi-studio-helperd.service" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/lib/systemd/system/genesi-studio-helperd.service"

    # ── tray autostart (skipped on KDE and GNOME, see the .desktop) ───────────
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/genesi-studio-tray.desktop" \
        "$pkgdir/etc/xdg/autostart/genesi-studio-tray.desktop"

    # ── icon ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # hicolor is the universal fallback, so the name resolves in every icon
    # theme — the lesson from the Genesi Containers tray, whose icon rendered
    # broken until it was installed here.
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/genesi-studio.svg" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/genesi-studio.svg"
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/genesi-studio.svg" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/genesi-studio-symbolic.svg"

    # ── Plasma 6 widget ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    local plasmoid="$pkgdir/usr/share/plasma/plasmoids/org.genesi.studio"
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/plasmoid-studio/metadata.json" \
        "$plasmoid/metadata.json"
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/plasmoid-studio/contents/ui/main.qml" \
        "$plasmoid/contents/ui/main.qml"

    # ── GNOME Shell extension ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    local ext="$pkgdir/usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/genesi-studio@genesios.org"
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/gnome-extension/metadata.json" "$ext/metadata.json"
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/gnome-extension/extension.js"  "$ext/extension.js"
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/gnome-extension/stylesheet.css" "$ext/stylesheet.css"

    # ── docs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    install -Dm644 "${startdir}/README.md" \
        "$pkgdir/usr/share/doc/genesi-studio/README.md"
}
